# Testing and Integration Patterns

## Unit Testing
- Place unit tests in [tests/](mdc:tests/) directory
- Use `#[cfg(test)]` for test-only code
- Mock external dependencies using the `mocks` feature
- Test both success and error paths thoroughly

## Integration Testing
- Integration tests are in [integration_tests/](mdc:integration_tests/)
- Use Ruby/RSpec for high-level integration testing
- Test real protocol communication with mock inverters
- Validate MQTT message handling and routing

## Test Fixtures
- Store test data in [integration_tests/fixtures/](mdc:integration_tests/fixtures/)
- Use JSON fixtures for packet data and responses
- Maintain separate fixtures for different test scenarios
- Document fixture format and purpose

## Mock Infrastructure
- Use the proxy system in [integration_tests/proxy/](mdc:integration_tests/proxy/) for testing
- Mock inverter responses for predictable testing
- Test error conditions and edge cases
- Validate protocol compliance

## Test Organization
- Group related tests in separate spec files
- Use descriptive test names that explain the scenario
- Test both happy path and error conditions
- Validate async behavior and timeouts
